From: Catalyst Linux
Subject: [PATCH] panel-mipi-dbi-m: sleep the panel while it is blanked

The pipe's disable only switched the backlight off; the ST7789 went on
driving its glass. Display off and sleep in take it from milliamps to
microamps. Enable already runs the panel's whole init sequence (the bus
is write-only, so the panel is never found on and is always set up
afresh), which starts with sleep out.

--- a/modules/st7789v-1.0/panel-mipi-dbi-m.c	2026-11-20 16:32:27.234106725 -0800
+++ b/modules/st7789v-1.0/panel-mipi-dbi-m.c	2026-11-20 16:32:27.234106725 -0800
@@ -426,6 +426,13 @@
 
     mutex_lock(&panel->display_lock);
     mipi_dbi_pipe_disable(pipe);
+    /*
+     * Catalyst Linux: blanked, the panel sleeps (microamps rather than
+     * milliamps). Enabling it again runs the whole init sequence, which
+     * begins with sleep out, as at boot.
+     */
+    mipi_dbi_command(&dbidev->dbi, MIPI_DCS_SET_DISPLAY_OFF);
+    mipi_dbi_command(&dbidev->dbi, MIPI_DCS_ENTER_SLEEP_MODE);
     mutex_unlock(&panel->display_lock);
 }
 
